## Pad with zeros

To add zeros at the start of values in *Receipt No*, you first need to convert the column’s data type to string (text) and then use the Polars expression `zfill`, like this:

::: {#97b3eb5b .cell execution_count=2}
``` {.python .cell-code}
(df
 .with_columns(pl.col('Receipt No').cast(pl.String).str.zfill(length=4))
 )
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}
```{=html}
<div><style>
.dataframe > thead > tr,
.dataframe > tbody > tr {
  text-align: right;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
}
</style>
<small>shape: (4, 2)</small><table border="1" class="dataframe"><thead><tr><th>Customer</th><th>Receipt No</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>str</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;Serena&quot;</td><td>&quot;0001&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Blair&quot;</td><td>&quot;0002&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Dan&quot;</td><td>&quot;0021&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Vanessa&quot;</td><td>&quot;0153&quot;</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
```
:::
:::


::: {.callout-note}
Setting `length=4` means the final value will have 4 digits. It **does not** mean the number of zeros to add.
:::

